[{:db/id "q-3594/selection/2c18b69cbdbee844ef52e47873ee9fb16194736518bddcc75da08c34625a809c" :answer/id #uuid "f3069168-8472-5f18-8c58-88afe4d3a8c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+4)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3594/selection/507cfb06c0091122bec4d0411cbd3d0b5236df49ea88ff41eb3207438440141a" :answer/id #uuid "f7c17e01-1d2e-5286-b250-057a8f4e234a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x-4)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3594/selection/d156c4b0c942e702a743f9c691b2c9847c055c1bbf1fcfe6213b939c3ba69f50" :answer/id #uuid "b16746dc-71a3-5df9-9acc-a8074ecba670" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{4})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3594/selection/af09eddb83b94da6ed0cb3df47a40ca8f36aff50b49c6c85a72f025109b76efe" :answer/id #uuid "361b89aa-276a-5bc5-9ba4-dae54d4cad5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+4)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3594/selection/9bfb958c5d0876c4baf5e18b97bba52255aa95f8f501be0202c2217ba3c3ca4a" :answer/id #uuid "9af19106-c603-5dce-947e-84a6b3c0053e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{4})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3594/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "470baffa-4a10-5421-986b-935a9babb4df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3594/selection/af09eddb83b94da6ed0cb3df47a40ca8f36aff50b49c6c85a72f025109b76efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-3594/selection/2c18b69cbdbee844ef52e47873ee9fb16194736518bddcc75da08c34625a809c" "q-3594/selection/507cfb06c0091122bec4d0411cbd3d0b5236df49ea88ff41eb3207438440141a" "q-3594/selection/d156c4b0c942e702a743f9c691b2c9847c055c1bbf1fcfe6213b939c3ba69f50" "q-3594/selection/af09eddb83b94da6ed0cb3df47a40ca8f36aff50b49c6c85a72f025109b76efe" "q-3594/selection/9bfb958c5d0876c4baf5e18b97bba52255aa95f8f501be0202c2217ba3c3ca4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3594" :question/id #uuid "e3fdf05c-295a-5e89-9088-f77e5fcdcab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-3594" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-8x-15}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-8x-15 & =-({x}^{2}+8x+15) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+[{4}^{2}-{4}^{2}]+15) \\\\  & =-((x+4)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-(x+4)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-8x-15}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-8x-15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+4)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-3594/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6e4cf3-803a-5942-9ce0-7047942e078a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3594"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114929/selection/93da0448c5c2081aa8a6b9b52453b37bd68166d2df7dbe7c7105ffb404cdb02a" :answer/id #uuid "5da2310b-5147-55e0-9fce-869491551d87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114929/selection/8bf777a562a5400fa08c0692cf455320e44936c3fbeda49c5ef7cb49fb2b8e2f" :answer/id #uuid "69459a5a-78bd-5a75-a710-151ba7bc7369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(2(x+2))+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114929/selection/b0549dd7e3ca04cd870c97dac03d5cc99bfa457138173817c949602b1d86f631" :answer/id #uuid "ea6c089c-5a2d-5f98-b34a-4994f73412e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114929/selection/1fd4bff55c0316ef057d3bf8d20e053c56e54ec0a294c9764819d7ef6168aef8" :answer/id #uuid "a5ea4255-4890-53fa-8093-78c3d5c90e20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114929/selection/7e91bb8de1833a7a0afb997b36a52ddead913a4089638b03e23973abb3a29dec" :answer/id #uuid "303e3a0c-27e8-5798-84d6-ec42d1c1dbd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-2}{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114929/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2a3b181-ecac-5f9e-830e-fbde4956fc1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114929/selection/1fd4bff55c0316ef057d3bf8d20e053c56e54ec0a294c9764819d7ef6168aef8" :answer-field/choices ["q-114929/selection/93da0448c5c2081aa8a6b9b52453b37bd68166d2df7dbe7c7105ffb404cdb02a" "q-114929/selection/8bf777a562a5400fa08c0692cf455320e44936c3fbeda49c5ef7cb49fb2b8e2f" "q-114929/selection/b0549dd7e3ca04cd870c97dac03d5cc99bfa457138173817c949602b1d86f631" "q-114929/selection/1fd4bff55c0316ef057d3bf8d20e053c56e54ec0a294c9764819d7ef6168aef8" "q-114929/selection/7e91bb8de1833a7a0afb997b36a52ddead913a4089638b03e23973abb3a29dec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114929" :question/id #uuid "81c55570-629f-5396-8873-462527b0ef2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114929" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+3 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+3 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+4x+4)-4+3 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x+2.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114929/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d1dc808-1ee6-5037-b53e-9e1e4686a11c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114929"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348528/field-1/e7e505d325c3cadeeeaf26a0afda20aaa10bea508f9739931632d1057683cd77" :answer/id #uuid "18f57394-9cc8-5d07-93b8-8daa12845952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348528/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer/id #uuid "b4e64174-5c3a-5877-a1d8-12099e9e6e96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348528/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb331360-19da-55a4-acd4-d5e2c70f1b7a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348528/field-1/e7e505d325c3cadeeeaf26a0afda20aaa10bea508f9739931632d1057683cd77" :answer-field/choices ["q-348528/field-1/e7e505d325c3cadeeeaf26a0afda20aaa10bea508f9739931632d1057683cd77" "q-348528/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348528" :question/id #uuid "318a8320-1013-5c6f-87d1-585357c4540e" :question/math-academy-id "q-348528" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}-3}^{-1}\\frac{6}{|x+3|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+6x+8}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+8 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+8 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+8 \\\\  & =(x+3)^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}-3}^{-1}\\frac{6}{|x+3|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+6x+8}}\\,\\text{d}x=6{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}-3}^{-1}\\frac{1}{|x+3|\\sqrt{(x+3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{2}-3$ | $-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}-3}^{-1}\\frac{6}{|x+3|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+6x+8}}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}\\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =6(\\text{arcsec}(2)-\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2})) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348528/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d1dc808-1ee6-5037-b53e-9e1e4686a11c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348528"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348555/field-1/82a873b6b3ece3b4059b2da1839886387bbd4d4e56d0ad136fc169204f9d3030" :answer/id #uuid "716ae010-e0f1-5a5d-8b29-57097da9c2cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348555/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "85050299-9eba-534f-9d3b-a1b37edc9626" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348555/field-1/82a873b6b3ece3b4059b2da1839886387bbd4d4e56d0ad136fc169204f9d3030" :answer-field/choices ["q-348555/field-1/82a873b6b3ece3b4059b2da1839886387bbd4d4e56d0ad136fc169204f9d3030"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348555" :question/id #uuid "45bc44ce-a438-5f0a-9306-145d75ddb29f" :question/math-academy-id "q-348555" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+8x+17 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+17 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+17 \\\\  & =(x+4)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{(x+4)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x+4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348555/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa497df-853e-5e77-9d43-6183fa53ffff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348555"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348571/field-1/d06063337828ee1b6e96bf391c602d22322b28d341de087000694ae32405eefb" :answer/id #uuid "a12ea5c9-2503-591d-b3a3-530a28b3ca34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348571/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cefbaf5e-2df5-5659-8c31-ce88cbd9f39b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348571/field-1/d06063337828ee1b6e96bf391c602d22322b28d341de087000694ae32405eefb" :answer-field/choices ["q-348571/field-1/d06063337828ee1b6e96bf391c602d22322b28d341de087000694ae32405eefb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348571" :question/id #uuid "41d50ccc-6fda-5b39-8eea-3178955d6238" :question/math-academy-id "q-348571" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{5}^{5+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}-10x+26}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10x+26 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+({5}^{2}-{5}^{2})+26 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2})-25+26 \\\\  & =(x-5)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7}{{x}^{2}-10x+26}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{7}{(x-5)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-5).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $5+\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{5+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}-10x+26}\\,\\text{d}x & =7{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =7(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =7(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348571/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa497df-853e-5e77-9d43-6183fa53ffff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348571"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
